{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.748c9d0d0f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data6-285","passage":"<p>The library will ______ laptops to students for up to two weeks.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["lend","borrow","donate","purchase"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “lend,” meaning give temporarily. “Donate” (give to a cause) doesn't fit. “Purchase” (buy) doesn't fit. “Borrow” (take temporarily) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.f60d0eb7c9","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data6-287","passage":"<p>Without counting, can you ______ how many people are in the crowd?</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["verify","assume","estimate","measure"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “estimate,” meaning roughly calculate. “Measure” (find the exact size of) doesn't fit. “Assume” (suppose without proof) doesn't fit. “Verify” (check that something is true) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.e52b110c72","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data6-293","passage":"<p>Cactus plants can ______ weeks without water.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["pity","tolerate","admire","envy"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “tolerate,” meaning put up with. “Pity” (feel sorrow for) doesn't fit. “Admire” (respect and approve of) doesn't fit. “Envy” (wish one had what another has) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.f1424bc719","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-295","passage":"<p>In the study, the amount of sleep was the only ______ that researchers deliberately changed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["hypothesis","variable","conclusion","sample"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “variable,” meaning factor that can change. “Conclusion” (judgment reached after reasoning) doesn't fit. “Hypothesis” (proposed explanation to be tested) doesn't fit. “Sample” (group selected for study) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.3595b288d1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-299","passage":"<p>When temperatures drop below zero, water trapped in cracks can ______ and split the rock apart.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["freeze","erupt","deposit","erode"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “freeze,” meaning turn to ice. “Deposit” (lay down material) doesn't fit. “Erode” (wear away gradually) doesn't fit. “Erupt” (burst out suddenly) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.d1c1a86ab7","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-303","passage":"<p>The ______ herders moved their camps several times a year in search of fresh grazing land.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["agrarian","urban","nomadic","industrial"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “nomadic,” meaning moving from place to place. “Agrarian” (relating to farming) doesn't fit. “Industrial” (relating to manufacturing) doesn't fit. “Urban” (relating to cities) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.64517a53cd","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-305","passage":"<p>Hundreds of students marched to the capitol in a ______ against the tuition increase.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["strike","petition","protest","boycott"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “protest,” meaning public demonstration of objection. “Boycott” (refuse to buy or use) doesn't fit. “Strike” (refuse to work) doesn't fit. “Petition” (formal written request) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.7173af21c9","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-305","passage":"<p>Consumers agreed to ______ the company's products until it improved conditions for workers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["protest","boycott","strike","petition"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “boycott,” meaning refuse to buy or use. “Petition” (formal written request) doesn't fit. “Strike” (refuse to work) doesn't fit. “Protest” (public demonstration of objection) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.405233a94a","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-307","passage":"<p>A textbook that summarizes other historians' research is ______ source.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a primary","a secondary","a biased","an objective"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “secondary,” meaning based on other sources. “Biased” (unfairly favoring one side) doesn't fit. “Primary” (firsthand) doesn't fit. “Objective” (not influenced by personal feelings) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.764c1a06ed","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-313","passage":"<p>The country's farms ______ most of their coffee to Europe and North America.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["subsidy","export","commerce","tariff"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “export,” meaning send goods abroad for sale. “Commerce” (buying and selling) doesn't fit. “Tariff” (tax on imports) doesn't fit. “Subsidy” (government payment to support an industry) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.d0ae2dcc75","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-319","passage":"<p>Workers will ______ a new bridge across the river over the next two years.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["collapse","reinforce","construct","dismantle"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “construct,” meaning build. “Reinforce” (strengthen) doesn't fit. “Dismantle” (take apart) doesn't fit. “Collapse” (fall down) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.838e558fb7","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-323","passage":"<p>One cup of water per day is ______ for the small cactus.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["deficit","insufficient","sufficient","excess"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “sufficient,” meaning enough. “Deficit” (shortfall) doesn't fit. “Insufficient” (not enough) doesn't fit. “Excess” (more than needed) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.6553461b06","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-325","passage":"<p>______ Egyptians built the pyramids more than four thousand years ago.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["Modern","Medieval","Ancient","Futuristic"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “ancient,” meaning very old. “Futuristic” (suggesting the future) doesn't fit. “Modern” (relating to the present) doesn't fit. “Medieval” (relating to the Middle Ages) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b9fe1e16f5","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-333","passage":"<p>In the novel, the green light across the bay is a ______ of the character's hopes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["setting","theme","motif","symbol"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “symbol,” meaning something that represents an idea. “Theme” (central message) doesn't fit. “Setting” (time and place of a story) doesn't fit. “Motif” (repeated element in a work) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b276580c02","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-333","passage":"<p>Birds are a recurring ______ in the poet's work, appearing in nearly every poem.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["setting","theme","symbol","motif"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “motif,” meaning repeated element in a work. “Theme” (central message) doesn't fit. “Symbol” (something that represents an idea) doesn't fit. “Setting” (time and place of a story) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.e0f85a4a90","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-333","passage":"<p>The ______ of the novel is a small fishing village in 1850s Maine.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["symbol","setting","motif","theme"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “setting,” meaning time and place of a story. “Symbol” (something that represents an idea) doesn't fit. “Motif” (repeated element in a work) doesn't fit. “Theme” (central message) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.7357e2daa7","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data7-335","passage":"<p>The stock market is ______, with prices shifting every second.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["static","linear","dynamic","circular"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “dynamic,” meaning constantly changing. “Linear” (proceeding step by step in a straight line) doesn't fit. “Circular” (returning to its starting point) doesn't fit. “Static” (unchanging) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.54ba643882","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-340","passage":"<p>The cat seemed perfectly ______, purring quietly in the warm window.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["cautious","content","careless","curious"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “content,” meaning satisfied. “Careless” (not taking enough care) doesn't fit. “Curious” (eager to learn) doesn't fit. “Cautious” (careful to avoid danger) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.24436f6b23","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-341","passage":"<p>Could you ______ me your umbrella? I'll bring it back tomorrow.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["invest","contribute","withdraw","lend"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “lend,” meaning give temporarily. “Contribute” (give to a shared effort) doesn't fit. “Invest” (put money into for profit) doesn't fit. “Withdraw” (take back or remove) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.9d1242eb75","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-342","passage":"<p>The gymnast is so ______ that she can touch her toes to the back of her head.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["flexible","fragile","durable","transparent"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “flexible,” meaning easily bent. “Fragile” (easily broken) doesn't fit. “Transparent” (see-through) doesn't fit. “Durable” (long-lasting) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.e5744cd23c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-346","passage":"<p>The clown was hired to ______ children at the birthday party.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["inform","discourage","entertain","persuade"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “entertain,” meaning amuse. “Discourage” (try to prevent) doesn't fit. “Persuade” (convince) doesn't fit. “Inform” (give facts to) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.88c289c2b9","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-350","passage":"<p>The invitation says the dinner is ______, so guests should wear suits and gowns.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["elaborate","simple","formal","casual"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “formal,” meaning following official rules. “Casual” (relaxed and informal) doesn't fit. “Elaborate” (detailed and complicated) doesn't fit. “Simple” (plain and easy) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.0613fcc2cc","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-350","passage":"<p>The recipe is ______, requiring only three ingredients and five minutes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["casual","elaborate","simple","formal"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “simple,” meaning plain and easy. “Casual” (relaxed and informal) doesn't fit. “Formal” (following official rules) doesn't fit. “Elaborate” (detailed and complicated) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.4c04c289d5","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-360","passage":"<p>To ______ water during the drought, residents were asked to take shorter showers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["recycle","consume","generate","conserve"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “conserve,” meaning protect from waste. “Consume” (use up) doesn't fit. “Recycle” (convert waste for reuse) doesn't fit. “Generate” (produce) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.7e7d2729d3","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-364","passage":"<p>Experts spent two years working to ______ the faded mural.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["auction","restore","archive","exhibit"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “restore,” meaning repair to original condition. “Archive” (store records) doesn't fit. “Auction” (sell to the highest bidder) doesn't fit. “Exhibit” (display) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.baba02b155","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-368","passage":"<p>Without his glasses, the words on the sign looked ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["faint","vivid","distinct","blurry"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “blurry,” meaning unclear in outline. “Faint” (weak and hard to see or hear) doesn't fit. “Vivid” (bright and clear) doesn't fit. “Distinct” (clearly noticeable) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.a9942a5235","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-370","passage":"<p>After surgery, his ______ took three months of physical therapy.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["recovery","symptom","diagnosis","treatment"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “recovery,” meaning return to health. “Symptom” (sign of illness) doesn't fit. “Treatment” (medical care) doesn't fit. “Diagnosis” (identification of illness) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.82181844ce","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"group":"wic-wic_data8-374","passage":"<p>The steps must be completed in the correct ______, or the machine will not start.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["interval","duration","frequency","sequence"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “sequence,” meaning order in which things follow. “Interval” (period between events) doesn't fit. “Duration” (length of time) doesn't fit. “Frequency” (how often something happens) doesn't fit."}
